            <h2>Detailed Feature Breakdown</h2>

            <h3>1. ChatGPT Integration (Killer Feature)</h3>
            <p><strong>Why DALL-E 3 is Easiest to Use</strong></p>

            <p>DALL-E 3's ChatGPT integration is revolutionary for casual users:</p>

            <ul>
                <li><strong>Natural language:</strong> "Make it more vibrant" or "Add a sunset" instead of learning syntax</li>
                <li><strong>Automatic prompt enhancement:</strong> ChatGPT expands your simple request into a detailed prompt</li>
                <li><strong>Iterative refinement:</strong> "Make the sky darker" → ChatGPT generates a new version</li>
                <li><strong>Context awareness:</strong> ChatGPT remembers your conversation and preferences</li>
            </ul>

            <p><strong>Example workflow:</strong></p>
            <ol>
                <li>You: "Create a cozy coffee shop scene"</li>
                <li>ChatGPT generates a detailed prompt and image</li>
                <li>You: "Make it evening time with warm lighting"</li>
                <li>ChatGPT adjusts and regenerates</li>
            </ol>

            <p>This is infinitely easier than Midjourney's <code>/imagine</code> commands or Stable Diffusion's technical setup.</p>

            <h3>2. Image Quality & Photorealism</h3>
            <p><strong>Excellent for realistic images</strong></p>

            <p>DALL-E 3 excels at photorealism:</p>

            <ul>
                <li><strong>Realistic people:</strong> Natural faces, proper anatomy (mostly)</li>
                <li><strong>Detailed scenes:</strong> Complex compositions with multiple elements</li>
                <li><strong>Lighting & materials:</strong> Accurate light physics, realistic textures</li>
                <li><strong>Coherent objects:</strong> Objects that actually make sense structurally</li>
            </ul>

            <p><strong>Where it falls short vs Midjourney:</strong></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Less artistic/cinematic flair</li>
                <li>Sometimes "flatter" color palettes</li>
                <li>Less stylized aesthetics</li>
            </ul>

            <p>For photorealistic business/marketing images, DALL-E 3 equals Midjourney. For artistic/stylized work, Midjourney wins.</p>

            <h3>3. Text Rendering in Images</h3>
            <p><strong>Good but not best-in-class</strong></p>

            <p>DALL-E 3 improved text rendering significantly over DALL-E 2:</p>

            <ul>
                <li><strong>Short text:</strong> 1-3 words usually render correctly</li>
                <li><strong>Simple fonts:</strong> Clean, readable typography</li>
                <li><strong>Logos/signs:</strong> Decent for basic text elements</li>
            </ul>

            <p><strong>Limitations:</strong></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Long sentences often have spelling errors</li>
                <li>Complex typography (decorative fonts) struggles</li>
                <li>Not as reliable as Ideogram (which specializes in text)</li>
            </ul>

            <p>For designs requiring perfect text (posters, logos), use Ideogram. For occasional text elements, DALL-E 3 is adequate.</p>

